# Intent: The face has a fixed zone (owner decision 2026-11-16): y 28 to 184 of the 320 by 240 screen, laid out once and never moved or scaled for the banner above it or the subtitles below it. The default skin gets a transparent holder of that rectangle inside its whole-screen panel (so touches and swipes work everywhere as before); the holder clips what leaves it. Style offsets are from the middle of the zone (screen y 106). Big eyes is the approved design at 0.82 (eye 79 by 85, brows 7 px); Eyes only, Stock, Classic and Minimal keep their sizes; every eye top is at y 32 or lower, every mouth is centered at y 162 (the stock bar at 152) and its tallest open shape ends by y 180; the thinking dots sit at the mouth's place; the external gaze range is 10 px (was 16) and the mouth's own offset 2 px (was 8); the brows are pushed down so they never reach above the eye line; an eye's vertical offset (pose, gaze and drift together) is clamped so its lit shapes stay inside the zone. A core test checks 47,000 shape boxes over every style, emotion, lid, blink, voice level and gaze extreme. Colors: the screen behind the panel takes the face's background color, so the banner and subtitle zones match.
# Placement: unit (the face runs on the robot, so it is complete with no host)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_look_core.h and firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/default/{default.h,default.cpp,eyes.cpp,mouth.cpp} (ours, patches X01, V10 to V12, V20 to V22)
# Check after a flash: every style times every emotion drawn from the unit (scripts/fw-serial.py snap): nothing lit above y 28 or below y 184; the host renderer sheets and the zone check (scripts/fw-face-render, scene_banner.py) say the same.

